  "starterCode": "import torch, math\n\ndef inference_grouped_query_attention(Q: list, K: list, V: list, num_q_heads: int = 4, num_kv_heads: int = 2) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Implement Grouped-Query Attention (GQA)** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, math\n\ndef inference_grouped_query_attention(Q: list, K: list, V: list, num_q_heads: int = 4, num_kv_heads: int = 2) -> list:\n    t_q, t_k, t_v = torch.tensor(Q, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(K, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(V, dtype=torch.float32)\n    N, D = t_q.shape\n    d_k, G = D // num_q_heads, num_q_heads // num_kv_heads\n    q = t_q.view(N, num_q_heads, d_k).transpose(0, 1)\n    k = t_k.view(N, num_kv_heads, d_k).transpose(0, 1).repeat_interleave(G, dim=0)\n    v = t_v.view(N, num_kv_heads, d_k).transpose(0, 1).repeat_interleave(G, dim=0)\n    attn = torch.softmax(torch.matmul(q, k.transpose(-2, -1)) / math.sqrt(d_k), dim=-1)\n    return torch.round(torch.matmul(attn, v).transpose(0, 1).contiguous().view(N, D), decimals=4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
